---
import CodeTabs from '../../components/CodeTabs.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import FieldsTable from '../../components/openapi/FieldsTable.astro';
import ParamsTable from '../../components/openapi/ParamsTable.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="GET /revalidate">
  <p class="endpoint-badge">
    <span class="method">GET</span>
    <code>/revalidate</code>
  </p>

  <p>
    Refetch lyrics for a song that is already cached, and replace the cache entry when the content changed.
    This works for both found lyrics and cached "no lyrics" results. Requires a valid API key.
    It refreshes only the default TTML entry that <code>/getLyrics</code> serves.
  </p>

  <h2>Parameters</h2>
  <ParamsTable path="/revalidate" />

  <h2>Headers</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Name</th>
        <th>Required</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-API-Key</code></td>
        <td>Yes</td>
        <td>Valid API key. The endpoint works only when the server enforces API keys.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Example request</h2>
  <CodeTabs tabs={[
    { language: 'curl', code: `curl -H "X-API-Key: your-api-key" \\
  "https://api.betterlyrics.org/revalidate?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154"` },
    { language: 'javascript', code: `const res = await fetch("https://api.betterlyrics.org/revalidate?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154", {
  headers: { "X-API-Key": "your-api-key" },
});
const data = await res.json();` },
    { language: 'python', code: `import requests

res = requests.get(
    "https://api.betterlyrics.org/revalidate?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154",
    headers={"X-API-Key": "your-api-key"},
)
data = res.json()` },
    { language: 'go', code: `package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"io"
	"net/http"
)

func main() {
	req, err := http.NewRequest(http.MethodGet, "https://api.betterlyrics.org/revalidate?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154", nil)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	req.Header.Set("X-API-Key", "your-api-key")

	res, err := http.DefaultClient.Do(req)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	defer res.Body.Close()

	body, err := io.ReadAll(res.Body)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	fmt.Println(string(body))
}` },
  ]} />

  <h2>Success response</h2>
  <p>Status: <code>200 OK</code></p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "updated": true,
  "cacheKey": "ttml_lyrics:e85 don toliver octane 154s",
  "wasNegativeCache": false
}`}</code></pre>

  <p>
    When the upstream fetch fails or finds no lyrics, the status is still <code>200 OK</code>.
    The cache entry is not changed:
  </p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "no lyrics found from source",
  "updated": false,
  "cacheKey": "ttml_lyrics:e85 don toliver octane 154s"
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Response fields</h2>
  <FieldsTable path="/revalidate" describe={{ cacheKey: 'The cache key that was revalidated.' }} />

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You know lyrics now exist for a song that had none before</li>
    <li>The lyrics were corrected at the source</li>
    <li>You want to make sure you have the latest version</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Error responses</h2>

  <h3>Missing or invalid API key (401)</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "API key required for revalidation",
  "message": "Provide a valid API key via X-API-Key header"
}`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Missing parameters (400)</h3>
  <p>Both song and artist are required.</p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "song (s) and artist (a) parameters are required"
}`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Not in cache (404)</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "no cached lyrics found for this query",
  "cacheKey": "ttml_lyrics:unknown song artist"
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Only songs that are already cached can be revalidated. Other queries return <code>404</code>.</li>
    <li>The lookup uses the exact cache key for the query, with no duration tolerance. The key includes album and duration, so send the same four values you send to <code>/getLyrics</code>. Without them, the lookup usually returns <code>404</code>.</li>
    <li>Only the default TTML entry is refreshed. Entries for <code>/ttml/getLyrics</code>, <code>/kugou/getLyrics</code> and <code>/qq/getLyrics</code> are not changed.</li>
    <li>When the fetched lyrics replace a negative cache entry, the negative entry is removed</li>
    <li>The <code>updated</code> field is <code>false</code> if the content has not changed</li>
    <li>A valid API key is always required, so this endpoint is never rate limited (<code>X-RateLimit-Type: bypass</code>)</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
